0..75 Comment "// Streams as codata (#644): a family known by its observations, built by a"
76..148 Comment "// copattern block that answers each one, and taken apart by observing a"
149..223 Comment "// thunk of it. A recursive call claiming `>` is productive when it is the"
224..293 Comment "// whole arm of a copattern block: each observation yields before the"
294..366 Comment "// function runs again, so the fixpoint needs no termination claim. What"
367..426 Comment "// refuses is in `../../pathological/codata/streams.gandr`."
